  "body": "Part of #3663 (the tool library dialog). Step U10: the tool editor. After U8 (the dialog frame) and #898 (the tool fields). The largest step of the refit.\n\n## What happens\n\n![tool editor: mockup left, current right](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/toollib-compare/2-tool-editor.png)\n\n- The default preview is a 3D model, not a drawing to scale.\n- The Tool tab has no fields for Name, Tool number, Flutes, Helix angle, Tool material or \"Centre cutting\".\n- The holder section has a projection value, but no stick-out field, no check of the clamping range and no link to the holder.\n\n## Expected (mockup)\n\n- **Tool tab:** Name, Type, Tool number; group CUTTER (Diameter, Flute length, Corner radius, Flutes, Helix angle, Tool material, Centre cutting); group SHANK (Shank diameter). Values with units, through the form seam.\n- **Assembly group** (\"How this tool sits in a holder\"): Holder, **Stick-out**, Gauge length (derived, with the sum shown), a link **Open holder**, and a check line: \"The shank Ø10 is in the clamping range 3 to 20 mm\" (or a refusal by name). The component stack of #4271/#4280 stays in this group.\n- **Drawing:** a side view to scale is the default. It has dimension lines (gauge length, stick-out, flute, shank Ø, cutting Ø), the holder and the spindle nose outline. Check boxes: Dimensions, Holder, Flutes. The 3D view stays as an option.\n- Footer of U8: Duplicate, Cancel, Apply (one undo step).\n\n## Rules\n\n- Every edit is an undoable command; the drawing is built only when the tool changes (frame cost).\n- The \"Details\" tab shows the #898 fields.\n- Before and after screenshots in the PR body.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Tests: each new field lands through its command and undoes; stick-out changes the gauge length; a shank outside the clamping range shows the refusal; the drawing is not rebuilt on a still frame.\n- `layout_page_tool_editor` (or its current name) asserts the groups, the fields and the drawing check boxes.\n\nEffort: high (fields, a new drawing, the assembly checks and their tests).\n",
